--
-- #3132 (decided in #3012), slice 2 -- an assistant proposes a new membership
-- plan, and the person confirms in the app.
--
--   write  create_membership_plan  create_subscription_level (0637), the
--                                  command of the billing screen's "add level"
--                                  field (manageBilling, money on)
--
-- A membership plan is the assistant-facing word for a subscription level: a
-- percentage of the full subscription. The operation holds none of the
-- command's rules (the right, the money functionality, the registry's bounds,
-- the duplicate): it calls the command under the caller's identity, so the app
-- and the assistant can never disagree about what is allowed.
--
-- The target (mcp_target_create_membership_plan) asks the command itself
-- before anyone is asked: the command runs in a block that is always rolled
-- back, so a refusal is the command's own and nothing is written. It names the
-- percentage; the app adds the workspace. Its revision is the stored levels
-- document: a proposal made before the offer changed is stale. The command's
-- refusals reach the assistant as the dispatcher already maps them:
--   42501  denied / forbidden (the right, asked again after the confirmation)
--   55000  denied / not_exposed (the money functionality is off here)
--   22023  validation_error (a percentage outside the bounds, or none)
--   23505  validation_error before the confirmation, conflict after it (the
--          plan is already offered)

